    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived, read-only `contactPreference` field to the owner representation: `EMAIL` when an email is present, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nI followed the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner attributes (`locality`, `membershipLevel`, `initials`) rather than inventing a new mechanism:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `contactPreference` on the `Owner` schema as a read-only string enum (`EMAIL`/`PHONE`), matching how the other derived fields are documented. This drives the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a computed `getContactPreference()` getter (never persisted, derived from stored state), sitting beside the other derived getters. MapStruct maps it into the DTO by name automatically, so no mapper or endpoint changes were needed. I also extracted the shared email-presence check into a small private `hasEmail()` helper and reused it in `getMembershipLevel()`, avoiding duplicated logic.\n\nThe single-responsibility split holds: the rule lives on the entity as one small derived accessor, the schema documents it, and the existing mapper/response pipeline carries it out unchanged.",
